      "description": "The IRIS items this instance holds rather than merely names. The three worked examples are `wpr-rdo-2020-003-eng` (the WPRO publication style guide, and the worked example whose full DSpace item record drives the `iris-dspace` skill), `who-pub-tps-931` and `9789241548960-eng`. On 2026-10-30 (who-iris#107, the owner's \"pre-CDN preview\") every IRIS library the harness layers had ingested moved in beside them: twelve from the DAK layer (https://github.com/litlfred/smart-base; digital health guidance such as DIIG, the two classifications of digital interventions and the digital transformation handbooks) and three from the immunizations IG (the IMMZ DAK, 9789240016514 and DDCC:VS). Those layers now cite them as `{instance: \"who-iris\"}`. They are the `materialized` end of the catalogue -- every other node under `catalogue/nodes/` is `referenced`, and the entries here are what a materialization actually looks like. `milnorlink` is NOT here and never was an IRIS item; it went to folio-assistant-sci (bean r1lz). The id is `library`, the CONVENTIONAL one, so this entry OVERRIDES the default rather than joining it: overrides match on id and never on path, so a distinct id at the same path yields two entries for one directory and every fan-out consumer scans it twice. Measured while doing exactly that.",
